title: NPC_Dialogue
---
This is an example of a Yarn Spinner script. Write your dialogue here!
===
title:loadPhase
---
<<declare $dialogPhase = "">>
<<declare $hasVisited = false>>
<<setPhase NPC>>
//the NPC gameObject name called in the <<setPhase>> command should map to the SPECIFIC NPC you want to reference
//FOR INSTANCE: if you have a particular gameObject NPC that you want this to call from, make sure you're using that gameObject name
<<if $dialogPhase == "begin">>
<<jump Start>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "comeback">>
<<jump comeback>>
<<elseif $dialogPhase == "quest_completed">>
<<jump doneWithQuest>>
<<else>>
Nicholas: I'm not sure *what's* going on, but you dun' fucked up.
<<endif>>
===
title: Start
---
<<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
<<set $hasVisited to true>>
Nicholas: Hello there, stranger!
Nicholas: Nice to see you.
Nicholas: I have a lil' pickle that I need you to solve.
Nicholas: Can you help me?
    <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "pc">>
    ->Yes I can.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
        Nicholas: Great news! Thanks a bunch!
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
    ->Not right now, old man.
        <<getPhase NPC "comeback">>
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "npc">>
        Nicholas: Well... that hurts my feelings.
        <<cam_move NPC_Cam_Rig "return">>
===
title:comeback
---
Nichoals: Hey you're back! Did you change your mind?
Nicholas: Please, help me....!
    ->OK fine....
===
title:doneWithQuest
---
<<if $hasVisited == true>>
Nicholas: Did you finish the task I asked you to do?
    ->Sure did, hoss!
        Nicholas: That's great. I love you.
<<else>>
Nicholas: Heya! I see that you've got an item I've been looking for.
Nicholas: Can I take that off of your hands?
    ->Yeah, go for it pops!
        Nicholas: Gosh, you're the best. I love you.
<<endif>>
===